        "id": "604158712017349404_4",
        "username": "Shotgun",
        "cooked": "<p>Yes, that's how the free market works. You buy the things you want and/or need out of an abundance of choice that's available to all consumers.<br><br>Whining that every single product isn't made to specifically cater to you, and is going to fail just because the company isn't getting your money, is nothing but a display of low-intelligence entitlement, and is, quite frankly, a waste of your own time. It would serve you better to spend your time and money on bettering your own circumstances (such as by finding a more enjoyable game, or working on improving your grammar) instead of lecturing companies on how to generate revenue, like some armchair businessman.</p>",
